        "A soil profile is the vertical sequence of layers called horizons, exposed in a road cut or a pit. The dark A horizon holds most organic matter and roots; the B horizon accumulates clay leached from above; the weathered C horizon grades into parent rock. Nigerian upland soils often show deep, strongly leached profiles under high rainfall. Reading profiles is a field skill in {S}: horizon depth, colour and root lines tell you where to sample and how deeply roots can work.",
